ALVA — Interface Customization & Combat Feedback Update

Objective

Implement a polished interface customization and combat feedback update for Alva, using the existing architecture, visual design, combat systems, and settings infrastructure.

Repository: https://github.com/hiyroscript/alva

This update has two primary goals:

1. Make Launch Point recovery more visually recognizable by making the recovering Launch Point number glow green.
2. Introduce a new Interface settings category containing four independently configurable options:
    * Ability HUD
    * Cooldown indicators
    * Damage hints
    * Combat hints

Combat hints will display contextual floating messages such as Blocked, Deflected, and Stunned during gameplay.

All features must integrate cleanly with the existing engine. Do not introduce duplicate combat systems, change balancing, or redesign unrelated interfaces.

⸻

1. Launch Point Recovery — Green Glow

Required behavior

When a fighter’s Launch Point is actively undergoing passive recovery, their Launch Point number in the top HUD must glow green.

Alva already implements passive recovery in:

* js/game/combat/combat-state.js
* js/data/launch.js

The current behavior is:

* Receiving an unblocked hit increases Launch Point and resets its recovery timer.
* Recovery has an initial 2-second delay.
* After that delay, 1 Launch Point is removed every 0.5 seconds.
* Recovery stops at 0.
* Blocking does not reset recovery.

Preserve these rules exactly.

Visual implementation

Modify the HUD in:

* js/ui/hud.js
* css/battle.css

The Launch Point number should behave as follows:

Normal state

Display the number with its current white appearance.

Recovery delay

For the initial 2 seconds after receiving damage, the number remains white. Recovery has not actively begun.

Active recovery

After the delay expires, while Launch Point is above 0 and passively recovering:

* Change the number to a clearly readable green.
* Add a soft green outer glow using CSS text-shadow.
* Use a restrained, smooth glow effect that fits Alva’s existing interface.
* Keep the number and its position unchanged.
* Update its displayed value as recovery progresses.
* Apply this independently to both fighters.

Suggested appearance:

* Bright green foreground.
* Soft, layered green glow.
* No green background, new bar, or additional HUD element.

Recovery interrupted

When a new unblocked hit resets recovery, immediately remove the green glow and return the number to its normal appearance until recovery resumes.

Fully recovered

Once Launch Point reaches 0, remove the glow entirely.

Technical requirements

Derive the visual recovery state from the existing CombatState recovery timer and Launch Point value.

For example, the relevant state already includes:

* combat.launchPoint
* combat.launchRecoveryRemaining
* LAUNCH_RECOVERY_DELAY
* LAUNCH_RECOVERY_INTERVAL

Do not determine recovery solely by comparing the currently displayed number to its previous value. That would miss the intervals between recovery ticks and could confuse healing effects with passive recovery.

If useful, introduce a clean read-only getter representing active Launch Point recovery.

In js/ui/hud.js, update the existing HUD number’s state class independently of the cached text value, so visual state changes register even when the number stays the same.

Use css/battle.css for the visual styling.

Respect reduced-motion settings. The green color and glow should remain understandable without animation.

The result must work in Quick Battle, Watch Mode, and Practice Ground, using the existing shared HUD.

